  "raw_text": "No. A filename alone cannot establish that two files are the same source-of-truth document.\n\nTo verify, compare:\n\n- File contents or cryptographic hashes\n- Version/revision identifiers and metadata\n- Creation and modification dates\n- Folder/repository provenance\n- Document owner or authoritative system\n- Digital signatures, audit logs, or version history\n\nAlso note that timestamps and filenames can be copied or changed. The authoritative source should be determined by provenance and content, not naming alone.",
